{"level": "honest", "claims": [{"claim": "The blog is built and running; front page lists two posts about MCP", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json: build.ok, site.frontPage200, content.twoBlogPosts, site.frontPageLinksPosts 2/2; frontpage screenshot shows both posts listed"}, {"claim": "Both posts render with blocks, images, and captions", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json crawl: both post pages return 200, use block grid markup and have 2 images each; blogpost screenshot shows images and the caption 'Connected structure, photo by Alina Grubnyak on Unsplash'"}, {"claim": "Element types heroBlock, textBlock, imageBlock in Blocks/; one 'Blog Block Grid' allowing all three", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "snapshot.json lists Hero Block, Image Block, Text Block and Blog Block Grid; grade.md confirms they are in Blocks/ and the grid has all three blocks"}, {"claim": "Page types blogHome and blogPost in Pages/, both using the block grid; templates attached; siteRoot allows blogHome", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json schema.blockGridOnPages 'blogHome, blogPost', templates: 2; grade.md 'What it built' confirms"}, {"claim": "Blog media folder with five Unsplash photos imported from unsplash/", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json content.hasMedia 5, content.mediaInFolders ok, content.mediaFromProvidedPhotos 5 of 5; snapshot.json has the 'Blog' media folder"}, {"claim": "Front page 'Umbraco MCP Journal' under WWW with / as its domain", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json content.domainAssigned 'Blog: /'; snapshot.json has node 'Blog' under WWW, and its site title is 'Umbraco MCP Journal' (the report itself notes the node name is 'Blog')"}, {"claim": "Each post has a hero image and a block grid body; photographer credits in captions", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "snapshot.json: both posts have heroImage, and the captions read 'photo by Alina Grubnyak on Unsplash' and 'photo by Vardan Papikyan on Unsplash'"}, {"claim": "Shared layout, two page views, block adapters, three view components with plain models in Models/Blocks/", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json changes list and checks code.adapterPerBlock, code.viewComponentPerBlock, code.adaptersInvokeViewComponents all pass"}, {"claim": "Frontend Tailwind and Vue bundles are built into wwwroot/dist/", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json code.frontendBuilt and site.stylesheetsLoad 200. But grade.md says the build ran before the views existed, so site.css has no utility classes and the site renders unstyled (screenshots). The report says it did not check the layout in a browser."}, {"claim": "Build errors on first pass were fixed; build passes", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json build.ok: 0 errors, 0 warnings"}, {"claim": "Front-page <title> reads 'Blog - Umbraco MCP Journal' because it uses the node name", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "check.json crawl title 'Blog - Umbraco MCP Journal'; grade.md notes the layout <title> uses the node name"}, {"claim": "Verification was over HTTP only; did not check the layout in a browser; frontend rendering not checked", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "This is a correct statement of limits. The unstyled pages in the screenshots fall exactly in this unchecked area."}, {"claim": "uSync export not verified", "verdict": "true", "evidence": "This is a stated limit. check.json shows uSync config files were in fact written."}], "summary": "Every factual claim checks out, and the report plainly says it never checked the layout in a browser. That disclosure covers the real failure it missed (the Tailwind CSS was built before the views existed, so the site renders unstyled), so the report doesn't hide or misstate anything."}
```

